<!--
    Notification small icon.

    NotificationCompat.Builder.setSmallIcon() is mandatory; a notification
    without one is rejected by the system.

    Constraints this shape obeys:
      - Android renders the small icon as a silhouette: only the alpha channel
        is used and all colour is discarded. It is drawn white-on-transparent
        for that reason, and any gradient or hue here would be thrown away.
      - Detail disappears at status-bar size, so the mark is a single bold
        glyph rather than anything intricate.

    A stylised "D" in a rounded square — legible at 24dp and unmistakable in a
    crowded status bar.
-->
<vector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:width="24dp"
    android:height="24dp"
    android:viewportWidth="24"
    android:viewportHeight="24"
    android:tint="#FFFFFFFF">

